# The repository is edited on Windows and built inside Linux, so line endings
# are decided here rather than left to whatever core.autocrlf happens to be on
# a given machine. A shell script that arrives with CRLF endings fails with
# "bad interpreter", which is a confusing way to learn about a checkout setting.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.ps1 text eol=crlf

*.img binary
*.gz binary
*.xz binary
*.cpio binary
